## 2.6. Gas adsorption ability
Gas adsorption isotherms were obtained by a Gemini VII2390 automated apparatus (Micromeritics, America) at 77 K. Samples $(0.1\mathrm{-}0.2\ \mathrm{g})$ was degassed by nitrogen $(\mathbf{N}_{2})$ blowing at $105~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for $^\mathrm{~1~h~}$ before adsorption testing. The BrunauerEmmett-Teller specific surface area (BETSSA) of filter samples were calculated by ${\bf N}_{2}$ adsorption isotherms at relative vapor pressures of $0.01{-}0.3\mathrm{MPa}$ (Yang et al., 2017).
